  "Description": {
    "Cost": 1130957,
    "UIName": "Kohlen",
    "Id": "chassisdef_kohlen_K-112",
    "Name": "Kohlen",
    "Details": "The Kohlen K-112 arms a rock cutter in the right arm capable of breaking down anything from pebbles to boulders, paired with a mining drill in the left arm for reaching deeper depths. Twin lift hoists, a searchlight and environmental sealing support deep mining operations. A small laser has been added to the left torso for extra flexibility.\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Quirk: Rugged</color></b>\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Drop Cost Multiplier: 0.87</color></b>",
    "Icon": "uixTxrIcon_Warlock"
  },
  "VariantName": "K-112",
  "ChassisTags": {
    "items": [
      "IndustrialMech",
      "mr-resize-1.09-0.97-0.93"
    ]
  },
  "StockRole": "Industrial Mech",
  "YangsThoughts": "The Kohlen comes from a long forgotten Terran Hegemony concern, built as a MiningMech capable of replacing entire teams of miners even in dangerous conditions. Its size works against it in tighter mines, but where it fits, it's usually a welcome sight, able to dig itself out of cave-ins with its own tools. 24 tons of industrial armor protect it from falling debris, though its rock cutter and mining drill have occasionally proven far more dangerous when turned against people rather than stone.",
